Package: rbpengine
Title: Relevance-Based Prediction (Thin R Client for RBP Math Engine)
Version: 1.3.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Cambridge Sports Analytics", role = c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Cel", "Kulasekaran", role = c("cre"),
           email = "ckulasekaran@csanalytics.io")
    )
Description: Open R client for the RBP Math Engine C ABI. Provides predict_rbp,
    predict_maxfit, and predict_grid with a PredictionResults nested list that
    mirrors the Python rbp_engine package. The package builds and installs without
    the private engine; prediction and insight entry points load the engine at
    runtime (RBP_ENGINE_LIB or a staged install under RBP_ENGINE_HOME /
    /Library/rbp-engine). Licensing uses rbp-license-info and standard license
    environment variables.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: utils, jsonlite
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), digest
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Optional RBP Math Engine runtime (shared library
    librbp_math_lib plus platform BLAS/LAPACK companions and license tools).
    Not required to install or load this package; required for prediction.
URL: https://cambridgesportsanalytics.r-universe.dev,
    https://docs.csanalytics.io/Install/R,
    https://github.com/CambridgeSportsAnalytics/rbp-engine-r
BugReports: https://github.com/CambridgeSportsAnalytics/rbp-engine-r/issues
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
